# Desktop backend packaging: keep the source files (spec/requirements/script)
# tracked even though the generic build/ rule above ignores them, but never
# track the build outputs or local venv.
!desktop/build/
desktop/build/*
!desktop/build/cowagent-backend.spec
!desktop/build/requirements-desktop.txt
!desktop/build/build-backend.sh
!desktop/build/build-feishu-vendor.py
!desktop/build/entitlements.mac.plist
!desktop/build/installer.nsh

# Icon authoring scratch dir: intermediate assets used to produce the final
# icons. Only the finished icons under desktop/resources/ should be committed.
desktop/resources/.icon-work/

# Bundled ripgrep binary: downloaded by CI (release workflow) at build time,
# never committed — it's a multi-MB platform-specific executable.
desktop/resources/bin/

.wrangler/

# Obsidian editor workspace (accidental commit vector; never part of the app)
.obsidian/

# FuXi session state (settings, scheduled-task locks, scratchpad symlinks)
.fuxi/

# Persistent Agent Mail credentials and npm runtime created by the optional compose overlay.
docker/agent-mail-data/

# --- Runtime state must never live in the source tree (P0-20 L-1) --------
#
# The memory index under <repo>/memory/long-term/index.db is RUNTIME STATE:
# it is a rebuildable projection of the knowledge base, and it belongs to
# whoever runs the app, not to the repository. It was found here because a
# run had the repository itself configured as the workspace root, so the
# index was written into the source tree -- and because it was neither
# tracked nor ignored, `git clone` handed every new user someone else's
# memory index (2.1 MB, 106 chunks of the shared knowledge base).
#
# The fix has two halves, and both are needed:
#   1. this file keeps the runtime products out of the repository, and
#   2. agent/memory/acceptance/phase1.py REFUSES to run against a workspace
#      that is inside the source tree, so the criterion cannot recreate it.
#
# Rule: if you find yourself wanting to commit one of these, the thing you
# want to commit is the SOURCE, not the state.
#
# The patterns are ANCHORED to the repository root on purpose. A bare
# `memory/` also matches `agent/memory/` -- and a newly created file there
# would be silently ignored, so the acceptance criteria could never be
# committed. Anchoring keeps `agent/memory/` trackable and ignores only the
# runtime state at the top level.
/memory/
/MEMORY.md
/tmp_wx.txt

# CowAgent 的**工作区骨架**也是运行时状态，同一个病根：
# 有一次运行把仓库本身当成了工作区根，于是它把自己的身份文件
# (AGENT.md / USER.md / RULE.md / BOOTSTRAP.md) 和知识库 (knowledge/)
# 写进了源码树。这些不是本仓库的源码 —— 本仓库是「跑 CowAgent 的东西」，
# 不是「CowAgent 的工作区」。
/AGENT.md
/USER.md
/RULE.md
/BOOTSTRAP.md
/knowledge/

